    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0771" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg677"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 108.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Department’s note of the 14th
                    ultimo, presenting affidavits as to the destruction by the insurgents in Cuba of
                    the property of Patricio Ponce de Leon, an American citizen, I have now the
                    honor to inclose copies of additional affidavits stating that further and
                    serious destruction of his property has been carried on both by the insurgents
                    and the Spanish soldiery.</p>
                <p>I also beg to call your attention to his affidavit that, while other neighboring
                    plantations have been protected by detachments of Spanish soldiers, he has been
                    unable to secure protection for his property.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
